From: shircomay <112399495+shircomay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:50:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(milakit): add ParagraphTranscriptFormatter for
 speaker-paragraph Markdown

Groups a transcript's segments into speaker paragraphs with one timestamp
each, for transcripts that are read as text (knowledge bases, notes) rather
than played as subtitle cues. Pure and dependency-free, like the rest of
MilaKit.

- Only adjacent segments of the same speaker group; a returning speaker
  starts a new paragraph. Segment order is preserved.
- A paragraph also breaks after a soft word cap (180, only at segment
  boundaries) and after a long pause (4 s), so undiarized recordings do not
  become one wall of text.
- A paragraph's timestamp is its first segment's own start, never borrowed
  from a later one; an invalid start renders as "[time unavailable]".
- Spoken text is emitted verbatim. Only speaker labels are escaped, and only
  text that would open a line as Markdown block syntax gets a guard.

